# oracle: fix adapt on pair colloid d1 of the 1-1 pair (pair_coeff refuses d1 != d2 for I,I, fix adapt does not): native init_one writes a1 and a2 from d1 and then d2, so both radii of the 1-1 pair stay d2/2, while d2 of the 1-2 pair changes its radius; 30 steps of nve
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-10 abs=1e-10
units           lj
atom_style      atomic
lattice         sc 0.001
region          box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 9.0
mass            2 1.0
set             group all type/fraction 2 0.5 4321
velocity        all create 1.0 87287 loop geom
pair_style      colloid 12.0
pair_coeff      1 1 144.0 1.0 5.0 5.0 12.0
pair_coeff      1 2 75.4 1.0 4.0 0.0 8.0
pair_coeff      2 2 39.5 1.0 0.0 0.0 2.5
variable        d equal 0.6
variable        e equal 1.2
fix             1 all nve
fix             2 all adapt 0 pair colloid d1 1 1 v_d pair colloid d1 1 2 v_e scale yes
timestep        0.002
thermo_style    custom step temp pe press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             30
